From 040b5145b11bb9d5c5ea2bb5abf41f77a3153c37 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 04:56:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Prediction by linear extrapolation of the previous time step

New prediction strategy LINEAR_EXTRAPOLATION_PREDICTION: the increment of
the unknowns of the last time step accepted is extrapolated, weighted by
the ratio of the time increments, then the values imposed by the Dirichlet
boundary conditions at the end of the time step are applied. No linear
system is solved.

The extrapolation is only made at the first resolution of a time step, the
first call to solve which follows update or revert: the following
resolutions of the same time step start from the current estimate, as
with the default prediction. The reference of the relative criterion of the
non linear solver remains the norm of the residual of the default
prediction, computed by one integration of the behaviours without tangent
operator and one evaluation of the residual per time step: the criterion
does not depend on the prediction. Without previous time step, the default
prediction is used, without this cost. The strategy is refused when the non
linear solver of PETSc is selected globally: it can't receive this
reference.

With the other strategies, the resolutions are unchanged.

Test LinearExtrapolationPredictionTest, with the Newton solver, the fixed
point on the elastic operator and the NewtonK0 method: values of the
prediction and ratio of its residual to the reference on a linear problem,
first resolution of a time step only, extrapolation made again after
revert, increment released by another strategy, no iteration when the
displacement is proportional to the time, same solution with fewer
iterations on a plastic cube.
